1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,750
Hello!

2
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:04,421
This week you will learn four reading techniques:

3
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:10,416
skimming to get the main idea, scanning to find details, recognising paraphrase,

4
00:00:10,416 --> 00:00:13,788
and telling True, False, and Not Given apart.

5
00:00:15,088 --> 00:00:15,526
First:

6
00:00:15,526 --> 00:00:19,610
skimming, which means reading quickly for the main idea.

7
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:25,590
Read the title, the first sentence, and often the last sentence of each paragraph.

8
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:27,341
Don't stop at new words.

9
00:00:27,341 --> 00:00:33,832
Then write three to five words next to each paragraph, so you know where to come back to.

10
00:00:35,132 --> 00:00:39,645
Read the title and the first sentence of each paragraph.

11
00:00:39,645 --> 00:00:41,660
Do not stop at new words.

12
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:44,966
Second:

13
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:48,215
scanning, which means searching for a detail.

14
00:00:48,215 --> 00:00:50,959
Decide first what you are looking for:

15
00:00:50,959 --> 00:00:56,303
a capitalised name, a number, a date, or a keyword that is hard to change.

16
00:00:56,303 --> 00:01:00,852
When you find it, read the sentence or two around it carefully.

17
00:01:02,152 --> 00:01:04,946
Scan for names, numbers and dates.

18
00:01:04,946 --> 00:01:09,136
Then read the sentence around the answer carefully.

19
00:01:11,936 --> 00:01:12,394
Third:

20
00:01:12,394 --> 00:01:13,233
paraphrase.

21
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:17,352
Questions rarely use the exact words from the passage.

22
00:01:17,352 --> 00:01:22,463
Expect synonyms, a change of word class, active changed to passive,

23
00:01:22,463 --> 00:01:25,591
or an idea expressed in the opposite way.

24
00:01:25,591 --> 00:01:32,456
If a question copies the passage word for word, check carefully, because it may be a trap.

25
00:01:33,756 --> 00:01:36,937
Free of charge means costs nothing.

26
00:01:36,937 --> 00:01:39,301
Only a few means not many.

27
00:01:39,301 --> 00:01:42,300
She decided becomes her decision.

28
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,152
Fourth:

29
00:01:46,152 --> 00:01:47,965
True, False, Not Given.

30
00:01:47,965 --> 00:01:51,356
True means the passage says the same thing.

31
00:01:51,356 --> 00:01:54,667
False means the passage says the opposite.

32
00:01:54,667 --> 00:02:01,211
Not Given means there is not enough information to confirm or reject the statement.

33
00:02:01,211 --> 00:02:06,336
Watch out for limiting words such as all, most, only, and almost.

34
00:02:07,636 --> 00:02:09,090
The passage says:

35
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:11,313
Only a few tickets remain.

36
00:02:11,313 --> 00:02:12,938
The statement says:

37
00:02:12,938 --> 00:02:15,076
Plenty of tickets remain.

38
00:02:18,376 --> 00:02:19,857
The passage says:

39
00:02:19,857 --> 00:02:22,382
The museum opened a new cafe.

40
00:02:22,382 --> 00:02:24,037
The statement says:

41
00:02:24,037 --> 00:02:26,824
The cafe serves vegetarian food.

42
00:02:30,124 --> 00:02:32,159
Answers to the two examples.

43
00:02:32,159 --> 00:02:37,682
The first is False, because only a few and plenty of have opposite meanings.

44
00:02:37,682 --> 00:02:39,426
The second is Not Given,

45
00:02:39,426 --> 00:02:44,803
because the passage only says there is a new café and never mentions food.

46
00:02:44,803 --> 00:02:48,364
Even if it sounds reasonable, you must not guess.

47
00:02:49,664 --> 00:02:51,321
Three common mistakes.

48
00:02:51,321 --> 00:02:51,622
One:

49
00:02:51,622 --> 00:02:56,592
choosing False just because the passage doesn't mention something,

50
00:02:56,592 --> 00:02:59,302
when the answer should be Not Given.

51
00:02:59,302 --> 00:02:59,604
Two:

52
00:02:59,604 --> 00:03:04,347
using outside knowledge instead of relying only on the passage.

53
00:03:04,347 --> 00:03:04,799
Three:

54
00:03:04,799 --> 00:03:09,920
reading every word carefully from the start and running out of time.

55
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,576
Skim first, then scan.

56
00:03:12,876 --> 00:03:15,192
Mini quiz, three questions.

57
00:03:15,192 --> 00:03:21,194
For each one, you hear a short extract from a passage and a statement.

58
00:03:21,194 --> 00:03:24,024
Choose True, False, or Not Given.

59
00:03:24,024 --> 00:03:26,940
The answers are in the next scene.

60
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:28,594
One.

61
00:03:28,594 --> 00:03:30,100
The passage says:

62
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,959
Flash is not allowed.

63
00:03:31,959 --> 00:03:33,641
The statement says:

64
00:03:33,641 --> 00:03:35,324
Flash is permitted.

65
00:03:35,324 --> 00:03:35,678
Two.

66
00:03:35,678 --> 00:03:37,183
The passage says:

67
00:03:37,183 --> 00:03:41,345
The festival attracted a large crowd this year.

68
00:03:41,345 --> 00:03:43,027
The statement says:

69
00:03:43,027 --> 00:03:47,543
The festival was held for the first time this year.

70
00:03:47,543 --> 00:03:48,075
Three.

71
00:03:48,075 --> 00:03:49,580
The passage says:

72
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,590
Tickets cost nothing for students.

73
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:54,273
The statement says:

74
00:03:54,273 --> 00:03:56,752
Students can enter for free.

75
00:04:03,052 --> 00:04:03,648
Answers.

76
00:04:03,648 --> 00:04:03,946
One:

77
00:04:03,946 --> 00:04:08,118
False, because not allowed is the opposite of permitted.

78
00:04:08,118 --> 00:04:08,416
Two:

79
00:04:08,416 --> 00:04:12,587
Not Given, because the passage only says it was crowded,

80
00:04:12,587 --> 00:04:17,429
and doesn't say whether it was the first time the event was held.

81
00:04:17,429 --> 00:04:17,876
Three:

82
00:04:17,876 --> 00:04:22,420
True, because cost nothing is a paraphrase of enter for free.

83
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,284
Summary:

84
00:04:25,284 --> 00:04:31,551
for each passage, skim for two to three minutes, underline the keywords in the questions,

85
00:04:31,551 --> 00:04:36,551
scan to find the location, and then read the answer sentence carefully.

86
00:04:36,551 --> 00:04:42,537
Do the ten exercises in the app, then take the weekly test with two reading passages.

87
00:04:42,537 --> 00:04:46,059
The target is at least sixty-five percent correct.

88
00:04:46,059 --> 00:04:48,876
For every wrong answer, note the reason:

89
00:04:48,876 --> 00:04:52,608
vocabulary, a Not Given trap, or running out of time.
